Third-party interoperability
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Hibana interoperates with several existing reader ecosystems. Where compatibility
required matching an external API, package name, or file format, that surface was
implemented against the upstream project's public interface.

Mihon / Tachiyomi — Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/mihonapp/mihon
  The `eu.kanade.tachiyomi.*` classes under app/src/main/kotlin are a host-side
  runtime implementation of the Tachiyomi extensions-lib API. They exist so that
  extension APKs compiled against that API resolve at runtime. The `.tachibk`
  backup schema is likewise implemented to match the published wire format.

IReader — Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/IReaderorg/IReader
  Hibana depends on the published artifact `io.github.ireaderorg:source-api`
  rather than reimplementing it.

LNReader — MIT License
  https://github.com/lnreader/lnreader
  Hibana loads LNReader JavaScript plugins and provides the host modules those
  plugins import (`@libs/fetch`, `cheerio`, and related shims).

Manatan
  https://github.com/KolbyML/Manatan
  Manatan extensions use the Tachiyomi extension packaging and are loaded through
  the same runtime described above.

